===== proxxx stop --help =====
Stop a guest

Usage: proxxx stop [OPTIONS] [VMIDS]...

Arguments:
  [VMIDS]...
          Guest VMID(s)

Options:
      --force
          Force stop without graceful shutdown (PVE hard-kill — sends SIGKILL to the qemu process, container init)

      --strict
          

      --allow-risk
          Override proxxx pre-flight risk checks (lock, HA-managed, active network traffic, prod tag, …). Distinct from `--force`, which is PVE-level hard-kill semantics

      --stop-timeout <STOP_TIMEOUT>
          Seconds PVE waits for graceful shutdown before hard-killing the guest (QEMU: SIGKILL; LXC: init kill). Ignored when `--force` is set. [default: 60]
          
          [default: 60]

      --policy <POLICY>
          Execution policy: full (default), canary[=N%], rolling[=K]
          
          [default: full]

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Connection profile name

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (only in CLI mode)

          Possible values:
          - json
          - json-envelope: JSON wrapped in a envelope carrying the producing version (audit 2026-09-09, #284)
          - table
          - plain
          
          [default: table]

      --token-secret <TOKEN_SECRET>
          API token secret. **Visible in the process listing** (`ps`, `/proc/<pid>/cmdline`) for as long as the command runs, and in shell history and CI logs. Prefer `--token-secret-file`, `PROXXX_TOKEN_SECRET`, or the OS keychain — especially for `daemon serve`, which is long-running

