===== proxxx cloud-img download --help =====
Download a cloud image into a PVE storage via PVE's `download-url` (server-side SHA-256 verified). The bytes never transit through proxxx — PVE talks directly to the upstream over HTTPS.

Returns the task UPID. Use `proxxx tasks --node <node>` to follow progress; the typical 500 MiB image takes 30 s to a few minutes depending on upstream bandwidth.

Usage: proxxx cloud-img download [OPTIONS] --node <NODE> --storage <STORAGE> <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>
          Registry id (run `proxxx cloud-img list` for the catalog)

Options:
      --node <NODE>
          Target PVE node

      --storage <STORAGE>
          Target PVE storage. Must accept `content = iso`

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Connection profile name

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (only in CLI mode)

          Possible values:
