===== proxxx anomaly --help =====
Rolling-baseline z-score anomaly detection across nodes for CPU + memory. Exit 0 = clean, 1 = anomalies found

Usage: proxxx anomaly [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --threshold <THRESHOLD>
          Z-score threshold above which a sample is flagged as anomalous. Default 3.0 (~99.7th percentile for normal-ish distributions; aggressive enough to catch the obvious outlier, permissive enough not to fire on every burst)
          
          [default: 3]

      --min-cpu-delta <MIN_CPU_DELTA>
          Smallest CPU change, in percentage points of the node's CPU, that counts as an anomaly. On an idle node the history barely moves, so a 2-point blip can score z > 5; this keeps such noise out. A chosen default, not a measured one
          
          [default: 10]

      --min-mem-delta <MIN_MEM_DELTA>
          Smallest memory change, in percentage points of the node's RAM, that counts as an anomaly. A chosen default, not a measured one
          
          [default: 5]

      --output <OUTPUT>
          [default: text]
          [possible values: text, json]

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Connection profile name

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (only in CLI mode)

          Possible values:
          - json
          - json-envelope: JSON wrapped in a envelope carrying the producing version (audit 2026-09-09, #284)
          - table
          - plain
          
          [default: table]

