===== proxxx mcp serve-http --help =====
Start MCP HTTP server (Streamable HTTP transport, spec 2025-03-26)

Usage: proxxx mcp serve-http [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --bind <BIND>
          Address to bind (default: 127.0.0.1)
          
          [default: 127.0.0.1]

      --port <PORT>
          Port to listen on (default: 3000)
          
          [default: 3000]

      --token <TOKEN>
          Bearer token for auth (overrides `mcp_token` in config and survives SIGHUP reload). Visible in the process listing for as long as the server runs; prefer --token-file or `PROXXX_MCP_TOKEN`

      --token-file <PATH>
          Read the bearer token from a file; trailing whitespace is trimmed. Takes precedence over --token and `PROXXX_MCP_TOKEN`, which in turn win over `mcp_token` in config (#384)

      --insecure-bind
          DANGEROUS: allow binding to a non-loopback address WITHOUT auth. By default proxxx refuses to expose the MCP server on the network unless `mcp_token` (or --token) is set. Only pass this on a trusted network or behind an auth-enforcing reverse proxy

      --allowed-host <HOST[:PORT]>
          Additional Host/Origin authority (`<host[:port]>`) allowed on a non-loopback bind (repeatable)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Connection profile name

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (only in CLI mode)

          Possible values:
          - json
          - json-envelope: JSON wrapped in a envelope carrying the producing version (audit 2026-09-09, #284)
          - table
          - plain
          
          [default: table]

