===== proxxx patch --help =====
Cluster patching orchestrator (apt update + dist-upgrade + rolling reboot)

Usage: proxxx patch [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  plan          Show what would be upgraded across the cluster (apt update + list). No SSH required — pure API
  apply         Execute the patch plan. Requires `[profiles.X.ssh]` configured
  repositories  Show configured apt repositories on a node (sources.list + sources.list.d). Helps diagnose "why isn't this update visible to me" — usually a missing or disabled repo
  changelog     Plain-text changelog for one installed package on a node. Useful for "what's actually changed" before running `apply`
  versions      List every installed package on a node with version + state. Useful for kernel/manager-version drift across the cluster (`proxxx patch versions --node X | jq '.[] | select(.package=="proxmox-ve")'`)
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --profile <PROFILE>
          Connection profile name

