===== proxxx backup-jobs create --help =====
Create a new scheduled job. PVE auto-assigns the id; minimum required is `--schedule` + `--storage` + (`--all` OR `--vmid`). Use the web UI or `--raw KEY=VAL` for less-common knobs

Usage: proxxx backup-jobs create [OPTIONS] --schedule <SCHEDULE> --storage <STORAGE>

Options:
      --schedule <SCHEDULE>
          systemd-time format, e.g. `"mon..fri 02:00"`

      --storage <STORAGE>
          Target storage id

      --all
          Backup ALL guests (mutually exclusive with --vmid)

      --vmid <VMID>
          CSV of VMIDs to back up (mutually exclusive with --all)

      --mode <MODE>
          `snapshot` (default) | `stop` | `suspend`
          
          [default: snapshot]

      --compress <COMPRESS>
          `none` | `lzo` | `gzip` | `zstd`. PVE 7+ default is zstd

      --mailto <MAILTO>
          Email destination for run notifications

      --mailnotification <MAILNOTIFICATION>
          `always` | `failure` (default)

      --prune-backups <PRUNE_BACKUPS>
          Retention DSL — e.g. `keep-last=3,keep-daily=7`

      --comment <COMMENT>
          Free-form comment shown in the web UI

      --node <NODE>
          Restrict to one node (default: cluster-wide)

      --raw <RAW>
          Raw param escape hatch — repeatable `KEY=VAL`, forwarded to PVE verbatim. Example: `--raw exclude-path=/tmp/.*`

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Connection profile name

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (only in CLI mode)

          Possible values:
          - json
          - json-envelope: JSON wrapped in a envelope carrying the producing version (audit 2026-09-09, #284)
          - table
          - plain
          
          [default: table]

      --token-secret <TOKEN_SECRET>
          API token secret. **Visible in the process listing** (`ps`, `/proc/<pid>/cmdline`) for as long as the command runs, and in shell history and CI logs. Prefer `--token-secret-file`, `PROXXX_TOKEN_SECRET`, or the OS keychain — especially for `daemon serve`, which is long-running

      --token-secret-file <PATH>
          Read the API token secret from a file (audit #283).
          
          Unlike `--token-secret` this leaves nothing in the process listing. The file must be readable by this process; trailing whitespace is trimmed. Takes precedence over `--token-secret` when both are given, because it is the safer of the two and a caller passing both most likely means the file.

      --secure
          Require Telegram 2FA for destructive operations in the TUI; refuse destructive CLI commands (exit 8)

  -h, --help
