===== proxxx alerts --help =====
Alerting & notification routing (rule engine + Telegram/ntfy/webhook)

Usage: proxxx alerts [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  eval   One-shot evaluation of all configured rules. Prints events that would fire as JSON. Does NOT send. Use this in cron pipelines piped to your own notifier, or for `--dry-run`-style tests
  watch  Long-running daemon: poll cluster state every `--interval` and dispatch events through the configured channels. Dedup window per rule. Stop with Ctrl+C
  test   Send a synthetic test event to validate channel config end-to-end
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --profile <PROFILE>
          Connection profile name

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (only in CLI mode)

          Possible values:
          - json
          - json-envelope: JSON wrapped in a envelope carrying the producing version (audit 2026-09-09, #284)
          - table
          - plain
          
