===== proxxx vm create --help =====
Create a new QEMU VM from scratch. Returns the UPID — track via `proxxx tasks`. For cloning from a template, use `proxxx clone`

Usage: proxxx vm create [OPTIONS] --node <NODE>

Options:
      --node <NODE>
          Target node name

      --vmid <VMID>
          VMID (auto-assigned from cluster if omitted)

      --name <NAME>
          VM display name

      --memory <MEMORY>
          Memory in MiB
          
          [default: 1024]

      --cores <CORES>
          CPU cores
          
          [default: 1]

      --disk <DISK>
          Boot disk — `storage:sizeG` (e.g. `local-lvm:32`). Omit for diskless (e.g. net-boot)

      --iso <ISO>
          ISO image volid for CD-ROM (e.g. `local:iso/ubuntu-24.04.iso`)

      --ostype <OSTYPE>
          Guest OS type (l26, win11, other, …)
          
          [default: l26]

      --bridge <BRIDGE>
          Network bridge
          
          [default: vmbr0]

      --wait
          Wait for creation task to complete before returning

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Connection profile name

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (only in CLI mode)

          Possible values:
          - json
          - json-envelope: JSON wrapped in a envelope carrying the producing version (audit 2026-09-09, #284)
          - table
          - plain
          
          [default: table]

