===== proxxx ct --help =====
LXC container hardware/options management. Smaller surface than QEMU — no cloud-init, no VGA, etc. Same typed-vs-raw split as `proxxx vm`

Usage: proxxx ct [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  set         Update container hardware/options
  raw-set     Bypass typed flags and submit raw `key=value` pairs
  interfaces  Container network interfaces (PVE shells to `lxc-info` / `ip addr` in the container's netns). LXC equivalent of QEMU's QGA `network-get-interfaces` — works without an agent in the container
  create      Create a new LXC container from an OS template. Returns the UPID
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --profile <PROFILE>
          Connection profile name

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (only in CLI mode)

          Possible values:
          - json
          - json-envelope: JSON wrapped in a envelope carrying the producing version (audit 2026-09-09, #284)
          - table
          - plain
          
          [default: table]

