===== proxxx firewall --help =====
Firewall management. PVE has three rule scopes (datacenter, node, guest); pick one. Read inspection plus full CRUD for aliases, IP sets, and security groups (cluster + guest scope). Individual allow/deny rule add/remove is not yet implemented — edit those via the PVE web UI or `pvesh` for now

Usage: proxxx firewall [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  cluster  Datacenter-wide rules (apply to every node and guest)
  node     Rules attached to a single node's host iptables
  guest    Rules attached to a guest's NIC chain (resolved automatically from VMID — works for QEMU and LXC)
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --profile <PROFILE>
          Connection profile name

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (only in CLI mode)

          Possible values:
          - json
          - json-envelope: JSON wrapped in a envelope carrying the producing version (audit 2026-09-09, #284)
