===== proxxx storage --help =====
Storage content management (upload local file to a storage, delete content item by volid). Read-side (`ls storage`) lives at the top-level `Ls`; this tree handles writes

Usage: proxxx storage [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  upload  Upload a local file (ISO, CT template, disk image for import) to a storage. Destination filename defaults to local basename
  delete  Delete a content item by `volid`. Format: `<storage>:<type>/<file>` for files (e.g. `local:iso/ubuntu.iso`) or `<storage>:<vmid>/<disk>` for VM disks. Required: `--yes`
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --profile <PROFILE>
          Connection profile name

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (only in CLI mode)

          Possible values:
          - json
          - json-envelope: JSON wrapped in a envelope carrying the producing version (audit 2026-09-09, #284)
          - table
          - plain
          
          [default: table]

